From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_OVN_DECODE_INDEX, _INDEX_SCHED, _POOLS32

ai-engine 94b93e567 applied clean onto the pin stack (no conflicts). DECODE_INDEX=N:
decode windows of fewer than N rows score with shared key tiles and select with the
split select (glm_index_split.cuh, the port of prod-src select_split, Apache-2.0);
INDEX_SCHED: production's prompt scorer schedule (glm_index_sched.cuh, from prod-src
prompt_scores.cu, Apache-2.0); POOLS32: int32 pool gathers. Default off and bit-exact;
glm-index-ovn-check compares them against today's kernels. Third-party provenance is
kept in the .cuh headers per the repo rule.

Gates on pin+0001..0009: check-native-cuda-host green, whole-tree fmt green, lean
base-vs-head 0 new (era comment lines single-lined, attribution kept; the piece consts
moved beside ranges in cuda_forward.zig for the 600-line rule), fatbins green for the
touched .cu files.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0056: glm-index-ovn-check is registered, and the declarations it reads are pub

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- lean_check.py's DIRECT_GETENV/HIDDEN_GETENV: every TF_* setting this patch reads is a row of platform/environment.zig with a line in docs/environment.md, read through cuda.ovn or environment, never getenv. Rows: TF_GLM_OVN_DECODE_INDEX (u64), _INDEX_SCHED and _POOLS32 (flags).
- cuda_index.zig: Kernels.load keeps index-decode-windows' registry read of TF_GLM_INDEX_DECODE_FROM (profile.lookup) beside the new split and sched fields.
- glm-index-ovn-check joins glm_ovn_checks.zig (the check table), not main.zig: the fold created that file in reply-prefill, which this re-seat defers.
- source: work/fold/0013-index-sched-decode-pools32.patch

